# security-scan during a scan". K1 has no Codex NOVEL and no ALREADY_COVERED claim in pass 0001.

@@ CIS-K1-0001
disp: NOT_AN_INDEPENDENT_CONSTRAINT
nature: CONFIGURATION_DIRECTIVE (EditorConfig root marker)
appl: actor=EditorConfig-aware tooling; action=stop ancestor .editorconfig lookup; trigger=resolving settings for repository files; modality=CONFIGURATION FACT; scope=repository files; exceptions=nested .editorconfig files still apply; timing=settings resolution; enforcement=tool behaviour, not executed; loading=not an instruction file
compared: FG-K1-7df8f75e64
rationale: .editorconfig:5 'root = true' verified. Same assessment as the identical claims of the other five candidates: format-defined lookup marker scoping the registered formatting values (FG-K1-7df8f75e64), no agent obligation; both Claude runs classified it as implementation.
scenario: N/A as a constraint: repository values are unchanged by root=false; only unspecified properties from outside the repository could be inherited.
conf: MEDIUM
open_issue: Methodology: revisit with the other five root=true claims if Stage 2 counts configuration-inheritance boundaries as constraints.

@@ CIS-K1-U0001
disp: NOT_AN_INDEPENDENT_CONSTRAINT
nature: IMPLEMENTATION_DETAIL (lexical approximation in the containment helper)
appl: actor=lib.cjs relInside and its callers; action=return null for a contained path whose relative name begins with '..'; trigger=file under a directory whose name starts with '..'; modality=NONE (implementation predicate); scope=hook/checker path containment; exceptions=genuine traversal correctly rejected; timing=hook/check run; enforcement=static code read, not executed; loading=script code
compared: FG-K1-b4ccfc754e FG-K1-97190af064 FG-K1-4917489c4d
rationale: lib.cjs:88-94 verified (doc comment: 'returns null when it escapes the root'). Same lexical prefix approximation as in the other candidates; only directory names starting with two dots are misclassified and no instruction states or forbids this. Edge-case limitation of in-root resolution (FG-K1-97190af064), not a clause.
scenario: N/A as a constraint; effect: a manifest at '..cache/package.json' is treated as out of root.
conf: MEDIUM

@@ CIS-K1-0002
disp: DISTINCT_UNREPRESENTED_CLAUSE
nature: CHECKER_ACCEPTANCE_GATE (invalid package.json JSON is an error)
appl: actor=check-manifests.cjs (CLI and post-change dispatcher); action=report an error finding when a selected existing package.json is not valid JSON; trigger=checking a package.json; modality=CHECKER ERROR (CLI exit 1; hook feedback); scope=package.json manifests; exceptions=missing files return no finding; timing=check run; enforcement=static code read (lines 130-136), not executed; loading=script
compared: FG-K1-6bce8e2857 FG-K1-4a6d4edee1 FG-K1-3e3bd27c1f FG-K1-7d8a86c09f FG-K1-c1d46b03f7
rationale: check-manifests.cjs:130-136 verified. Both Claude runs noted 'invalid JSON is an error' only in IMPLEMENTATION coverage notes; the K1 groups cover when checks run (FG-K1-6bce8e2857), version rules (FG-K1-4a6d4edee1), NUL decoding and walks (FG-K1-3e3bd27c1f) and per-file argument handling (FG-K1-7d8a86c09f). An unparsable package.json fails the check even without any dependency violation, so this is an unrepresented designed acceptance gate (consistent with candidate K0's manifest-readability proposals).
scenario: package.json with a trailing comma and only exact versions: no registered rule is violated, the checker reports 'package.json is not valid JSON'.
conf: MEDIUM
proposal: CHECKER_ERROR | check-manifests run on an existing package.json | A package.json that is not valid JSON is reported as an error finding instead of being skipped.

@@ CIS-K1-0003
disp: DISTINCT_UNREPRESENTED_CLAUSE
nature: CHECKER_ACCEPTANCE_GATE (unreadable manifests are errors)
appl: actor=check-manifests.cjs checkFile; action=report an error finding when reading/parsing an existing selected manifest throws; trigger=checking an existing .csproj, Directory.Packages.props or package.json; modality=CHECKER ERROR; scope=recognised manifests; exceptions=missing files return no finding; timing=check run; enforcement=static code read (lines 163-172), not executed; loading=script
compared: FG-K1-3e3bd27c1f FG-K1-6e757edf58 FG-K1-6bce8e2857 FG-K1-475b4d42b1
rationale: check-manifests.cjs:163-172 verified: any exception from the per-type checker (read failure, undecodable text, malformed XML tag thrown by the reader) becomes an error finding. The Codex groups FG-K1-3e3bd27c1f (decoding rejects NUL input) and FG-K1-6e757edf58 (minimal XML reader) describe causes of such exceptions but not the resulting checker error; no group states that an unreadable manifest fails the check. Distinct gate, consistent with candidate K0.
scenario: An existing .csproj that the checker cannot read: instead of 'no findings' the checker reports 'manifest could not be read'.
conf: MEDIUM
proposal: CHECKER_ERROR | check-manifests run on an existing recognised manifest | A recognised manifest that the checker cannot read or parse is reported as an error finding ('manifest could not be read'), not as a clean result.

@@ CIS-K1-U0002
disp: NOT_AN_INDEPENDENT_CONSTRAINT
nature: IMPLEMENTATION_DETAIL / POSSIBLE ENFORCEMENT GAP (option terminator stops operand parsing)
appl: actor=classify-command.cjs npm/pnpm/yarn classifier; action=stop parsing words at a standalone '--', so later package operands are not classified; trigger=recognised package-manager command containing '--' before package operands; modality=NONE (parser limit); scope=PreToolUse exact-version gate for npm/pnpm/yarn; exceptions=earlier operands, removals, nameless updates and peer-bypass flags are still classified; timing=PreToolUse; enforcement=static code read (line 219), no command executed; loading=script code
compared: FG-K1-e32ee646e0 FG-K1-b8551d715e FG-K1-891a447fdc FG-K1-5baad49862
rationale: classify-command.cjs:217-249 verified: 'if (w === '--') break;' ends the loop before positional operands are collected, so 'npm install -- pkg' yields no 'dependency-version' finding while 'npm install pkg' does. The registered gate (FG-K1-e32ee646e0: install/add/update naming packages without an exact version are blocked) is unchanged; the terminator handling narrows its effective coverage but creates no obligation or permission in the instructions. Recorded as an enforcement-gap observation, not a clause; whether every package manager treats operands after '--' as packages is not verified.
scenario: N/A as a constraint; effect: 'npm install -- example-package' is not blocked by the exact-version gate according to static reading.
conf: MEDIUM
open_issue: Possible bypass of the exact-version PreToolUse gate through 'npm|pnpm|yarn <install> -- <package>' (static reading only; package-manager semantics and the full dispatcher path not executed). Relevant for Stage 3/4 enforcement analysis.

