@@ CIS-K1-0004
disp: DISTINCT_UNREPRESENTED_CLAUSE
nature: WORKFLOW REVIEW STEP (conditional lockfile review, frontend)
appl: actor=agent running the security-scan workflow; action=review lockfiles; trigger=frontend workspace exists and package integrity or unexpected dependency changes are relevant; modality=PROCEDURAL, conditional; scope=security-scan workflow via scan-layers.md (Kind WF); exceptions=only when relevant; timing=during the scan; enforcement=instruction only; loading=read by security-scan during a scan
compared: FG-K1-a53d83e2f2 FG-K1-d74f68ee1a FG-K1-046f535dc4 FG-K1-b9ee2a8a83
rationale: scan-layers.md:21 verified; no K1 group is anchored on this line. The Codex group FG-K1-a53d83e2f2 (line 17: dependency review covers source trust, direct/transitive, npm audit) and the lockfile maintenance/CI groups do not state lockfile inspection during a scan. Unrepresented conditional review step, consistent with the other candidates.
scenario: An unexpectedly changed lockfile is not inspected during the frontend dependency scan although npm audit runs.
conf: MEDIUM
proposal: PROCEDURAL (conditional review step) | security scan with a frontend workspace where package integrity or unexpected dependency changes are relevant | Review the lockfiles when package integrity or unexpected dependency changes are relevant.
